course: dictionary
lesson: 1247
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one is meant. Bunting is a good example: it can mean a row of flags, a small bird, or an old word for a thin cloth.
explain: Read this: «hold a joint street party with bunting, a bouncy castle and a tug of war». The party, the bouncy castle and the tug of war tell you that bunting means the strings of coloured flags. A bird would not fit there.
explain: Now try your meaning in the sentence. «Bunting with 5 triangle flags and 4 square flags» is about counting flags and their corners, so bunting here means a string of flags. Swap in your meaning and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Bunting (noun, uncountable) means rows of small coloured flags, often triangles, hung on a string for a party or celebration.
fact: A bunting (plural buntings) is a small seed-eating bird, such as the reed bunting or the corn bunting.
fact: Old meaning: bunting was once a thin cloth used to make flags.
fact: Bunting is seen at street parties, fêtes, sports days and festivals, especially in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: Useful phrases: «put up the bunting» and «a string of bunting».
exercise: «hold a joint street party with bunting, a bouncy castle and a tug of war.» What does bunting mean here? | A small seed-eating bird | *Rows of small coloured flags on a string | A thin cloth for a bed | A wooden fence around the park
exercise: Which sentence uses bunting to mean a bird? | *A corn bunting sat on the fence and sang | Mum put up the bunting before the party | The bunting was thin and old | We counted the bunting flags at the sports day
exercise: «Bunting with 5 triangle flags and 4 square flags: 5 × 3 = 15 and 4 × 4 = 16, so 15 + 16 = 31 corners.» How many corners do the 5 triangle flags have altogether? | 31 | 10 | *15 | 16
test: What is the old meaning of bunting? | A loud party song | A kind of cake | A tall tree in a park | *A thin cloth used to make flags
test: Which phrase means hanging the flags up? | *put up the bunting | a string of buntings in a cage | a corn bunting | reed bunting
exam: In the sentence «A reed bunting sang while the street was hung with bunting», what tells you the first bunting is a bird? | The word street | The word hung | The word while | *The word reed and the word sang
